<title>UK: Russian Black Sea, Baltic oil outlets reopen.</title>
<headline>Russian Black Sea, Baltic oil outlets reopen.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's leading oil outlets on the Baltic and the Black Sea reopened at the weekend after brief weather-related closures, a reliable shipping source said.</p>
<p>Black Sea terminal Novorossiisk reopened on Saturday afternoon after closing at 1010 local time on Friday because of high winds.</p>
<p>Latvia's Baltic port of Ventspils opened on Sunday morning after closing on Friday.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
